p-value is the truncated-Beta ratio
\deqn{p = \frac{\mathrm{mass}\{\theta \in I_E,\ \theta \le \theta_{obs}\}}{\mathrm{mass}\{\theta \in I_E\}}.}
No sampling, no burn-in, no mixing assumption.

